UID:10003639-1777280400-1777285800@nertamid.org
SUMMARY:Breakfast Conversation: Building Shared Society in Israel with AJEEC
DESCRIPTION:Join us for a special breakfast conversation on Monday\, April 27 at 9:00 AM at Temple Ner Tamid\, featuring two distinguished leaders from the Arab–Jewish Center for Equality\, Empowerment and Cooperation (AJEEC). \nWe are honored to welcome Kher Albaz\, Chair of AJEEC\, and Dr. Ilan Amit\, Co-CEO\, who will share insights from their work building Jewish–Arab partnership and strengthening communities across Israel. Founded more than two decades ago in the Negev\, AJEEC has grown into one of the largest civil society organizations within Arab society in Israel and one of the country’s leading organizations dedicated to fostering a shared society. Through partnerships with government ministries and local authorities\, AJEEC supports youth leadership\, expands employment opportunities for young Arab adults\, and builds long-term community resilience in dozens of communities throughout the country. Our speakers will discuss the current challenges in the Negev\, efforts to rebuild and strengthen shared society in the wake of October 7\, and the enduring legacy of Vivian Silver\, AJEEC’s co-founder\, whose vision continues through the Vivian Silver Center for Shared Society in Be’er Sheva. \nAll are welcome to join us for breakfast and conversation as we learn together about partnership\, resilience\, and hope. \nRegister Here!
URL:https://nertamid.org/event/breakfast-conversation-building-shared-society-in-israel-with-ajeec/
LOCATION:NJ
CATEGORIES:Adult Education
END:VEVENT
